      "id": 1,
      "text": "Mount Washington was first settled in 1692 and officially incorporated in 1779.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Washington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors George Washington, who was Commander‑in‑Chief of the Continental Army when the town was incorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Washington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mount Washington sits on a plateau in the Taconic Mountains, with Mount Everett—the highest point in the southern Taconic range—rising 2,602 feet near the town’s eastern border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Washington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Appalachian Trail enters Massachusetts at Mount Washington, turning east near the town’s border before heading into Egremont.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Washington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mount Washington State Forest and Mount Everett State Reservation together cover a large portion of the town’s landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Washington%2C_Massachusetts",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
